      "reply": "Prescription drug coverage is called Part D. With Original Medicare, drug coverage is separate—you would usually join a standalone Part D drug plan; with Medicare Advantage, most plans include drug coverage as part of the plan.\n\nThe important catch is that drug coverage is never just yes-or-no by route: each drug plan has its own list of covered medicines, pharmacy rules, restrictions, and costs. So when prescriptions matter, Original Medicare gives you one medical route plus a separate drug-plan choice, while Medicare Advantage often bundles them together in one plan.",
